// `Result` is built from its variants, `Result.Ok(v)` and `Result.Err(e)`
// (ERRATA E56). `ok` and `err` are instance methods, and calling one through
// the type is E0413 rather than a call with the argument as its receiver
// (gap 35).
public void main() {
    Result<int, String> good = Result.ok(1);
    Result<int, String> bad = Result.err("no");
    Result<int, String> fine = Result.Ok(2);
    print(fine.isOk());
}
